    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d284">

                <pb facs="0509" n="385" sameAs="frus:frus1923v02/pg385"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.51/1509: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The High Commissioner in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-03-10T13:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">March 10,
                                1923—1 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received March 11—11:40
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>31. President Borno informed me this morning that on further consideration he
                    finds that it would be a violation of the Constitution for him to appropriate
                    the $10,000 for the preparation of internal tax law et cetera, there being no
                    law covering this subject and referred me to letter of General Receiver who in
                    the case where $1,200 <pb facs="0510" n="386" xml:id="pg386"/> had been carried
                    in budget for commission to revise communal taxes had refused payment on the
                    ground that there was no law authorizing such commission and therefore violated
                    Constitution. President then said that funds for the necessary work desired by
                    Mr. Hord<anchor n="1" xml:id="d284-f1"/> could by the treaty properly be charged
                    to 5 percent fund as expenses of Financial Adviser’s office and that he
                    authorized such a charge at once.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Russell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d284-f1" n="1" xml:id="d284-f1-content">
                <p>John S. Hord, Financial Adviser of Haiti.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
